# Shared loop profile: call-analyzer (Days to Expiry / fiAnalyst)
# Used by: pr-loop (Ready) + scope-loop (Scoping)
#
# CRITICAL PRODUCT — never auto-land to main.
# REST queue only: label issues `ready` to enqueue.
# Board is human view only when ORCH_BOARD=0.

REPO=fstrauf/call-analyzer
REPO_DIR=/Users/fstrauf/01_code/call-analyzer

# 0 = agents do not update kanban (recommended). Selection is REST labels only.
ORCH_BOARD=0

# NEVER merge to main from the loop in this repo. Orchestrator opens/marks
# PRs ready; a human reviews and merges.
ORCH_AUTO_MERGE=0
ORCH_MERGE_VIA_PUSH=0

# Two-tier test gate (epic #1748): non-stacked issues fork from + PR against
# `dev`, not GitHub's real default branch (main). `dev` gets a lean per-PR
# gate (test:pr); the full pnpm test:all runs once at release
# (webapp/scripts/release-dev-to-main.mjs) before a human fast-forwards
# main. Stacked issues still override this via ORCH_BASE_BRANCH per
# issue_base_branch() — unaffected.
ORCH_BASE_BRANCH_DEFAULT=dev
# Stack-aware land (mode A): auto = gh stack merge when PR is in an open chain.
# Irrelevant while ORCH_AUTO_MERGE=0; still used if you temporarily enable land.
# ORCH_STACK=auto

# Call-analyzer-specific Grok skill (real-user QA + monorepo test gate).
# Override at launch if you intentionally want the generic skill.
ORCH_SKILL=/pr-orchestrator

# Main agent model: default (K2.7 Coding, from default_model in
# ~/.kimi-code/config.toml). K3 was tried here on 2026-09-09 — both k3-256k and
# k3 429'd ("engine is currently overloaded") on large-context calls across
# four runs; small requests passed. To retry K3 off-peak, use:
#   if [ "${ORCH_AGENT:-kimi}" = "kimi" ]; then
#     ORCH_CLI_ARGS="-m kimi-code/k3"   # or kimi-code/k3-256k
#   fi
# (kimi-only guard needed because grok/ori would reject the -m flag.)
# Subagents stay on K2.7 Coding via [secondary_model] force=true in config.toml.
